# Product scope

This app lets someone who already has an Evolution GO instance token connect that instance's WhatsApp. It is not an instance admin console.

Upstream API: `https://evogo.se7esistemassinop.com.br`. Spec: `/swagger/doc.json`. Auth header on upstream calls: `apikey` set to the instance token.

## Allowed upstream calls

Only these instance-token routes (`Auth`, not `AuthAdmin`):

- `GET /instance/status`
- `POST /instance/connect`
- `GET /instance/qr`
- `POST /instance/pair` (`phone` is required)
- `POST /instance/reconnect`
- `POST /instance/disconnect`

## Forbidden

Do not add UI, routes, or client methods for creating, deleting, logging out, proxy changes, force reconnect, logs, listing instances, or any other Evolution GO tag (messages, groups, users, license). `DELETE /instance/logout` unlinks the phone; it is out of scope even though it uses the instance token.

Advanced settings stay out until the user asks. They need an `instanceId` the status payload does not return.

The browser never calls Evolution GO and never sees the instance token after login. Express holds the token and proxies the calls above.
